# Remaining before / around launch

Implementation work lives in openspec/changes/add-course-marketplace/tasks.md.
This file tracks what is NOT covered there, plus a summary of the tasks there that are still open
(built but unverified, or blocked on outside input).

## Legal and business
- [ ] Lawyer: confirm consumer-law refund/withdrawal rules for online sales (7-day right?) and whether a refund policy is mandatory
- [ ] Accountant: who issues invoices (nota fiscal) per sale, tax treatment of a marketplace with no platform fee
- [ ] Write terms of use and privacy policy (LGPD)
- [ ] Decide the business model: there is currently no platform fee, so the platform earns nothing from sales

## Decisions still open
- [ ] Verify exact package versions against the stack skill (Next, React, Prisma, Express, Zod, Tailwind) before scaffolding
- [ ] Confirm assumptions I added: email verification required before buying/creating courses; progress kept through refunds; only admins delete courses; unpublishing keeps subscriber access
- [ ] Hosting choice for web, API and Postgres (web and API must share a parent domain for the session cookie)
- [ ] Backups and monitoring for Postgres and the renewal job

## Risks to retire early
- [ ] Asaas sandbox spike (tasks.md 7.1), partly done, findings in design.md. Still open: (a) set ASAAS_SPIKE_DEST_WALLET_ID in apps/api/.env to the wallet of a second sandbox account (not the CNPJ account's own) and re-run the split/refund-reversal check; (b) ask Asaas to enable sub-accounts on the sandbox account (CNPJ/MEI still gets 403 on POST /accounts); (c) decide how to handle boleto, which the API cannot refund (block it or refund manually)
- [ ] Move renewal scheduler from node-cron to a job queue (e.g. pg-boss) before running more than one API instance
- [ ] Check Bunny Stream limits and cost per minute against expected creator uploads

